<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Frigidus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">394</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Frigidus was fought on 5–6 September 394 by the river Frigidus, probably the Vipava in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a>. The eastern emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a> defeated the western usurper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eugenius">Eugenius</a> and his Frankish general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arbogast">Arbogast</a>, helped by a strong wind, the bora, blowing in his soldiers' favour. The victory reunited the empire for the last time and was celebrated as a triumph of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> over a pagan revival.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-frigidus.jpg" alt="Battle of the Frigidus" width="320" height="271" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Weikhard von Valvasor · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Janez_Vajkard_Valvasor_-_Bitka_med_Teodozijem_in_Evgenijem.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
